this was almost 20 years ago US and  British forces invaded Afghanistan  following the September 11 attacks on  the United States the goal to stop this  land from ever again being used as a  launch pad by al-qaeda for terrorism the  Taliban government that gave the group a  safe haven was forced out but it fought  back now the u.s. is preparing to make  peace with its enemy the deal with the  Taliban affects Britain - its troops  have fought and died here I asked a  former top commander if the sacrifice  had been worthwhile if this truce works  and the Taliban have seen the light of  the day and can be integrated in a  constructive way and there's no hint of  any more terrorists operations being  mounted from within Afghanistan then I  for one will say that this was a  necessary war which we fought well and  and the result has been a draw if not  the conventional victory we might have  hoped back in 2006 how does it feel to  be at this point of a peace deal between  the United States and the Taliban my  feeling is that it's we don't certainly  have to be ashamed from this if it will  work there's a lot of risk in this  though and we must be prepared to do  again with the Americans on our allies  what might be required for another few  years to remind the Taliban that we will  there's a line beyond which we won't go  the deal hinges around a gradual  withdrawal of US British and other NATO  forces in return  the Taliban agrees to a ceasefire and  direct talks with these people the  Afghan government it's a gamble that  Donald Trump promised his voters he'd  end what he's called endless wars in an  election year what better time to bring  thousands of US troops home not  everyone's convinced Victoria lost her  husband Lance Corporal James Bateman  when British forces surged  into southern Afghanistan in 2006 mixed  feelings really I think anything that  can bring pace to a region that's been  so unstable would be amazing I said  about however I think personally it's  doing a deal with the devil it's a  feeling shared by many here in  Afghanistan  most people have known nothing but war  few dare to believe the deal will really  bring peace  Deborah Haines Sky News
 

